# The Oregon Trail (PPSA19244) — accept the startup legal/EULA popup and continue.
#
# Timing is anchored to the game's FIRST PAD POLL, not process start.
#
# What the route drives: the title opens on `WBP_System_Disclaimer_Popup` ("Welcome to The Oregon
# Trail" + three legal links + a focused confirm button). The shipped `BP_EULA_Controller` closes
# that popup from its confirm path and calls `SetEULAChecked`, after which `L_GameloftSplash`'s level
# Blueprint creates `WBP_Splash_Gameloft` and its completion path opens `/Game/Maps/L_Main`.
#
# Why repeated Cross pulses rather than one press at a fixed offset: the popup's own appearance time
# moves with load timing, the confirm button may require a focus pass first, and each legal link
# opens a scroll page whose Cross is "continue". Surplus presses are harmless in all of those
# states, and every arm of an A/B therefore sees the same input stream. Verify what the guest
# actually read with PROSPER_PAD_SCRIPT_LOG=1.
3-4:cross
7-8:cross
11-12:cross
15-16:cross
19-20:cross
23-24:cross
27-28:cross
31-32:cross
35-36:cross
39-40:cross
